# CombatMode Release Flow

When asked to prepare a release, ship an update, or finalize a version:

- Use `RELEASE.md` as the canonical release procedure.
- Use `TESTING.md` for the smoke/regression pass.
- Verify WoW API compatibility with MCP tools before finalizing notes.
- Call out any user-impacting changes (bindings, CVars, settings migration) clearly.
- Ensure version/interface metadata changes are explicitly included in the change summary.
- Confirm `CombatMode/CombatMode.toc` `## Version` matches the new Keep a Changelog section in `CombatMode/CHANGELOG.md`.
- After editing **`CombatMode/CHANGELOG.md`**, run **`scripts/sync-changelog-to-lua.ps1`** (or VS Code task **Sync CHANGELOG.md to ChangelogData.lua**) so **`CombatMode/UI/Changelog/ChangelogData.lua`** matches the in-game changelog viewer.
- Run the full lint gate: `pre-commit run --all-files`.

Day-to-day **code** finishes (not only tagged releases) still require lint → TOC version bump → CHANGELOG update → changelog sync per `combatmode-change-checklist.mdc` / `AGENTS.md`.

If the request is not release-related, apply normal architecture/safety/checklist rules.
